WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.342
Can you tell whether a number divides exactly without doing the whole division?

00:00:04.992 --> 00:00:07.853
Today we are using divisibility rules.

00:00:08.073 --> 00:00:15.217
We will test digits, combine two conditions when needed, and explain what the result tells us about factors and remainders.

00:00:15.867 --> 00:00:20.817
Our learning goal is to use divisibility rules and explain why a test passes.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.226
Success criteria.

00:00:23.446 --> 00:00:25.911
I can choose the test for the divisor.

00:00:26.131 --> 00:00:29.374
I can use final digits or digit sums correctly.

00:00:29.594 --> 00:00:33.191
I can combine the tests for two and three to test six.

00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:36.824
Divisible means division leaves no remainder.

00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:39.755
For two, check the final digit is even.

00:00:39.975 --> 00:00:43.846
For five, it must end in zero or five; for ten, zero.

00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:46.597
For three or nine, test the digit sum.

00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:49.516
For four, test the final two digits.

00:00:50.166 --> 00:00:53.574
Is seven hundred and thirty-eight divisible by six?

00:00:54.224 --> 00:00:58.701
A number is divisible by six when it is divisible by both two and three.

00:00:58.921 --> 00:01:01.360
Its last digit, eight, is even.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:06.103
The digit sum is seven plus three plus eight, which is eighteen.

00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:08.827
Eighteen is divisible by three.

00:01:09.047 --> 00:01:13.694
Both tests pass, so seven hundred and thirty-eight is divisible by six.

00:01:14.344 --> 00:01:19.064
Is one thousand two hundred and forty-five divisible by five and by nine?

00:01:19.714 --> 00:01:23.203
It ends in five, so the test for five passes.

00:01:23.853 --> 00:01:26.007
Its digit sum is twelve.

00:01:26.227 --> 00:01:30.747
Twelve is not divisible by nine, so the number is not divisible by nine.

00:01:30.967 --> 00:01:35.710
Passing one divisibility test does not imply passing every other test.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:40.490
An even number is divisible by two, but not always by six.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:45.828
Fourteen is even, yet its digit sum is five, which is not divisible by three.

00:01:46.048 --> 00:01:49.155
To test six, both conditions must pass.

00:01:49.805 --> 00:01:52.871
Is three hundred and twelve divisible by four?

00:01:56.871 --> 00:01:59.329
The last two digits form twelve.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:04.533
Twelve is divisible by four, so three hundred and twelve is divisible by four.

00:02:04.753 --> 00:02:08.498
Check: four times seventy-eight is three hundred and twelve.

00:02:09.148 --> 00:02:12.808
Choose the rule for the divisor and explain each condition.

00:02:13.028 --> 00:02:16.054
Six needs both the two and three tests.

00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:22.701
Divisibility rules are shortcuts for exact-division decisions, and multiplication can confirm the result.

00:02:22.921 --> 00:02:26.329
Reflect on which model helped you and explain why.
